  "title": "Unified Title: NeoWorld-3 and NeoWorld-Pro",
  "summary": "NeoWorld-3 introduces a coding-agent framework for simulating interactive 3D worlds from visual observations, enabling low-level geometries and physics validation. NeoWorld-Pro redefines monocular scene reconstruction as procedural programming for embodied simulation, leveraging MLLMs for code synthesis and physics validation.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "NeoWorld-3 provides a structured, executable API for vision-language agents to visually inspect, edit, and refine code for 3D scene reconstruction.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "NeoWorld-Pro uses zero-shot reasoning and MLLMs to convert monocular images into executable programs for interactive 3D environments.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Both frameworks demonstrate improved geometric fidelity, physical readiness, and support for complex tasks like manipulation and stacking.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
